<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:44:39Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>UNICEF: 1 in 5 youths targeted by online sexual abuse</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b01dda797ecd78f388f6f4fb1035b17a5494a46db6e53f209536a67d9e9cd3d</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:44:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T00:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/unicef-1-in-5-youths-targeted-by-online-sexual-abuse/a-78654173--873685942f5a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/unicef-1-in-5-youths-targeted-by-online-sexual-abuse/a-78654173?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A survey of around 21,000 young people by the UN's agency for children has found that online sexual abuse of minors is on the rise.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Unity at last: Is Libya's damaging power struggle at an end?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d6358bac0bc31ca8ae0a85b4aa047cb4cf125deb099e0e405d17c2b7ba0af06</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T17:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/unity-at-last-is-libya-s-damaging-power-struggle-at-an-end/a-78758325--86802ffc3f54.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/unity-at-last-is-libya-s-damaging-power-struggle-at-an-end/a-78758325?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For over a decade, Libya has been split between two opposing governments. Elections, meant to end the rivalry and unite the country, are now scheduled within two years.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Macron visits Bayeux Tapestry with King Charles, PM Andy Burnham</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5110672aa9c79772db71c028bbb922a86037d96c73e8942a5ffd00e58a8b5097</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T16:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/macron-visits-bayeux-tapestry-with-king-charles-pm-andy-burnham/a-78772317--aa51d6580620.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/macron-visits-bayeux-tapestry-with-king-charles-pm-andy-burnham/a-78772317?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron is on a shorter-term visit to the UK than the renowned on-loan 11th century tapestry. He viewed the ancient artwork with the UK monarch and relatively new Prime Minister Andy Burnham.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US sanctions halt TOEFL and GRE tests in Iran, disrupting study plans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0fa32837fd23bdc5810c7612f66c907a5ad865e6e47f697952cee9fa6f7689c4</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T14:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-sanctions-halt-toefl-and-gre-tests-in-iran-disrupting-study-plans/a-78764639--4e7bec2b9a4e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-sanctions-halt-toefl-and-gre-tests-in-iran-disrupting-study-plans/a-78764639?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Students in Iran can no longer take TOEFL and GRE exams after a US sanctions exemption was suspended. Applicants say the move threatens university deadlines and adds costly travel obligations.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Guinea-Bissau referendum tests democratic future</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4d48cb89ce3777712e57feee6e824246298c4bbf18af6c109d55232f7264d8d1</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T13:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/guinea-bissau-referendum-tests-democratic-future/a-78646043--6b02fe75908c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/guinea-bissau-referendum-tests-democratic-future/a-78646043?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Following voter approval of a constitutional change that expands presidential powers, Guinea-Bissau faces renewed debate over legitimacy, civilian rule and democratic safeguards.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India rejects Hague ruling on Indus waters: What's next?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8ecfd94ff16a7905368e3e3e7369027a392c51f399010937ccf7564904ee83b1</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T13:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-rejects-hague-ruling-on-indus-waters-what-s-next/a-78753249--bf87f4a9f22b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-rejects-hague-ruling-on-indus-waters-what-s-next/a-78753249?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">By rejecting an international arbitration panel's ruling, New Delhi has cast fresh doubt on the future of the 1960 Indus Waters Treaty.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Armed men abduct Kenyan editor, employer suspects government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f684578ee3d8b275c1c79e15fec7a38d922b6bd1863f339fff1b10950dae855c</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T12:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/armed-men-abduct-kenyan-editor-employer-suspects-government/a-78721264--2f75912edea2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/armed-men-abduct-kenyan-editor-employer-suspects-government/a-78721264?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A newspaper editor in Kenya was kidnapped from a car late on Tuesday and then located near a dam far away a few hours later. The Standard paper said it suspected state involvement in an attempt to intimidate reporters.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU summons Russian envoy over failed Leipzig drone attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b2e72e44fc5dba11ff959ac70ad0bfc8a3f652fcd03eaad0caa12ce93cd3c0e</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T08:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-summons-russian-envoy-over-failed-leipzig-drone-attack/a-78687280--a6943ed869f3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-summons-russian-envoy-over-failed-leipzig-drone-attack/a-78687280?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU's foreign policy chief Kaja Kallas said the attempted attack had "all the hallmarks of state-sponsored terrorism." She said the EU was summoning a Russian envoy, with France announcing a similar step.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany says Russia behind attempted drone attack at Leipzig airport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:29153ed17d536f0651c695a1bc889b4c833faae0cdca3b358c25ec3fb245a8bc</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T22:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-says-russia-behind-attempted-drone-attack-at-leipzig-airport/a-78584589--38d4d0353c74.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-says-russia-behind-attempted-drone-attack-at-leipzig-airport/a-78584589?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Investigators believe an explosives-laden drone was deliberately targeting a Ukrainian cargo aircraft at Leipzig/Halle airport in early August. The German government said on Tuesday that it held Russia "responsible."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Congo's Ebola caseload tops 6,000 as concerns grow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3417219734c95bb59d7650726462d68ed58c316570ba26fdd9b363159a4c1688</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T18:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/congo-s-ebola-caseload-tops-6-000-as-concerns-grow/a-78638447--c2dd272f865b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/congo-s-ebola-caseload-tops-6-000-as-concerns-grow/a-78638447?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of Congo has surpassed 6,000 confirmed cases, with nearly 3,000 deaths. As the virus spreads, authorities are racing to contain one of the deadliest outbreaks in history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran fuel crisis deepens amid war and sanctions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:93fcd41e350f58cfd8d688fdf552bc30d3c5e508d56c9aeacabcd62e246e010d</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T14:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-fuel-crisis-deepens-amid-war-and-sanctions/a-78636429--f0b92944bdf3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-fuel-crisis-deepens-amid-war-and-sanctions/a-78636429?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Long lines at fuel stations are spreading across Iran as war damage, import constraints and new US sanctions squeeze supplies.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Mladic's death, Bosnia and Serbia's unfinished reckoning</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eca652077849b86bc795773946c7591f435b73bd830f3cb0e094be1d584f831b</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T13:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mladic-s-death-bosnia-and-serbia-s-unfinished-reckoning/a-78602733--19ecd75a4666.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mladic-s-death-bosnia-and-serbia-s-unfinished-reckoning/a-78602733?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The death of Ratko Mladic did not close a dark chapter of European history; it reopened old wounds. The ideology that created him lives on. The Dayton peace agreement ended the war, not the divisions that produced it.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Will Bangladesh join the Mecca defense alliance?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e11c8995e83716a5558e65e9a097754829981785a955e19464197b6bd973e298</id><updated>2026-09-03T04:43:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T12:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-bangladesh-join-the-mecca-defense-alliance/a-78613944--a9c557768a92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-bangladesh-join-the-mecca-defense-alliance/a-78613944?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While Bangladesh weighs the risks of signing the Mecca Joint Defense Agreement, experts warn that such a move could complicate relations with neighboring India.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
